A||N||1||cscougar||Matching Red Paint Color||||1||
Z||000000||cscougar||06-08-2000||09:20 PM||||I have a 1985 Red GT.  I am looking for a good match of the stock red on this car.  I need to find paint such as the Duplicolor or Plasticote paint in 12 oz cans.  Does anyone know the correct color of either of the above to match the stock 85 red?<P>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||Sage||06-08-2000||10:02 PM||||Take the paint code off the label on the drivers side inner fender(under the hood)into an auto paint supplier, and they can look it up for you.  Most can mix a spray bomb up for in any color you have.  <P>They should also have a scanner that they put right on your car, then feed the output into the computer and it spits out the formula to match what you have.  <P>On old paint, this is as close as you are going to get.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||3
